1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nobile Giuseppe Maria Buonaparte (31 May 1713, Ajaccio – 13 December 1763, Ajaccio) was a Corsican politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sebastiano Nicolo Buonaparte and his wife Maria Anna Tusoli (1690–1760).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1749, Giuseppe was the Delegate who represented the City of Ajaccio in the Council of Corte.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giuseppe_Maria_Buonaparte
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://www.napoleon-empire.net/en/bonaparte-family.php
2 CONT
2 CONT  BONAPARTE, Giuseppe Maria - Paternal grandfather
2 CONT
2 CONT Born on May 31, 1713, he was the son of Sebastiano Nicola Bonaparte and Maria Anna Tusoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married on March 5, 1741 at Ajaccio Maria-Saveria Paravicini, who gave him:
2 CONT two daughters (Maria Geltruda and Marianna) 
2 CONT and two boys: Carlo Maria, Napoleon's father, and Sebastiano.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1749, Giuseppe Maria represented the city of Ajaccio to the Corsican Council in Corte.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his widowed, he remarried in 1760 Miss Maria Virginia Alata (born February 5, 1725).
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away on December 13, 1763.
