1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotta_Napoleona_Bonaparte
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT After the fall of her uncle Emperor Napoleon in 1815, her father moved to America and purchased "Point Breeze", an estate on the Delaware River near Bordentown, New Jersey. Charlotte and her sister, however, stayed with their moth
2 CONC er in Europe. They lived in Frankfurt and Brussels in 1815-1821, and then in Florence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notables like these had friends and assistants whose stories are often lost.  One family that did not lose the story Charlotte's long time nures https://www.geni.com/people/Amanda-Maillard/6000000085047531870?through=6000000085047
2 CONC 376055, her daughter https://www.geni.com/people/Amanda-Maillard/6000000085047531870?through=6000000085046366511 and her son-in-law https://www.geni.com/people/Eloy-Milliard/6000000180096277856?through=6000000085047531870.  who se
2 CONC ttled in Illinois in 1841 after Charlotte's death.  See story in Illinois Quest article attached as "Media"
2 CONT
