2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_II_of_France#Life
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Napoleon II (Napoléon François Joseph Charles, 20. maaliskuuta 1811 – 22. heinäkuuta 1832), Reichstadtin herttua, oli Napoleon Bonaparten poika ja lyhyen aikaa Ranskan keisari.
2 CONT
2 CONT Napoleon II, syntymästään Rooman kuningas, syntyi Pariisissa keisari Napoleon I:n ja hänen toisen vaimonsa arkkiherttuatar Marie-Louisen poikana. Kolme vuotta myöhemmin Ranskan ensimmäinen keisarikunta kuitenkin lyötiin, ja Napole
2 CONC on luopui kruunusta poikansa hyväksi, jonka keisarinna vei Château de Bloisiin huhtikuussa 1814. Napoleon luopui toisenkin kerran kruunusta poikansa hyväksi hävittyään Waterloossa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edustajien ja aatelin kamari tunnusti prinssi Franzin keisariksi välittömästi hänen isänsä luopumisen jälkeen 22. kesäkuuta 1815, mutta liittoutuman armeijoiden saapuminen Pariisiin päätti tämän vallan 7. heinäkuuta. Napoleon II:k
2 CONC si häntä ei kuitenkaan yleisesti kutsuttu. Tästä huolimatta seuraava keisari otti Napoleon III:n nimen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vuoden 1815 jälkeen prinssiä pidettiin Itävallassa. Hän sai Reichstadtin herttuan arvonimen 1818. Hän kuoli tuberkuloosiin Schönbrunnin linnassa 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Czesław Malewski, Rody i herby szlacheckie na Litwie (XV). 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archiwum2000.tripod.com/522/malews.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT Below we will describe an interesting story: the three famous properties of the French Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte (1769-1821), his son Napoleon II ( full name Napoleon François Charles Joseph Bonaparte ) (1811 Paris - Vienna, 1832
2 CONC ), and the famous French poet Guyom Apolinero (in French. Guillaume Apollinaire ) (1880-1918)  The connections as well as the role here was Melanija Kostrowitz  (Kostrovickaite /  Kostrowicka) who was the great granddaughter of Ba
2 CONC rbara Sekliuckytė. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The shoelaces have been associated with Kostrowitz, whose prominent representative is the famous French poet Apoliner, namely Apolinist Kostrowicki. Barbora Sekliuckytė with her second husband Samuel Kostrovickiu (1729 - 1780) had
2 CONC  a son Onufrijų ( Onufr ) (~ 1760 -?) and grandson Samuel (1788-1859). Samuel Kostrovicki and his wife, Ona Zaleskaya ( Anna Zaleska ) had a daughter named Melanja.. Melanija was educated in the literature, history, languages, mus
2 CONC ic and painting. She  was taken to Vienna's estate, Schloss Schönbrunn where lived the second wife of Napoleon, Napoleon second wife was  Marie - Louise d'Autriche (1791 1847).
2 CONT
2 CONT  Here Melanja met Napoleon and Marie Luis's son Napoleon II;  the second emperor of France, who was nicknamed Ereliukas. The Napoleonic marriage with the daughter of the Austrian Emperor Francis II was purely political which sough
2 CONC t to converge with the Hapsburg dynasty and have a successor. Immediately after his birth, his son received the title of Roman king, but Napoleon in 1814 and 1815 having left him the throne of the emperor in France, did not receiv
2 CONC e much approval.  The state winners resisted them. Ereliukas ruled only 15 days - since 1815 June 22 until 1815 July 7.  The damsel grew up in the Grandfather's Palace in Vienna where he was given Reichstadt (Reichstadt Duke's tit
2 CONC le) up until 1830. Ereliukas did not know who his real father was. The hopes of Napoleon II were tied by Bonapartists but in 1830 was overthrown by King Charles X of France, Napoleon II was already too weak to take on the throne, 
2 CONC He was sick and died early (21 years old). His pompous mask is exhibited at the Vienna Schonbrunn Palace.
2 CONT
2 CONT  One day Melanija and Ereliukas got acquainted. The eaglet Melanija old age is pasakojusi nephew Marcelijus     (Marcin ) Kostrovickiui (brother Lucian, who was married to Jozefa Sekliuckytę ( Jozefa Sieklucka ), son), it gives hi
2 CONC m not only for his oil paintings, but also drawings, watercolors and oil painted works with Reichštato Duke's signature. Melanija and Erelius became lovers.  Here a son was born to Melanija (who was 18 years old)  born in Italy, f
2 CONC inding herself  with explainable circumstances. The kidnapper - a child of the Imperial Blood - was arranged and educated (for the money of Kostriewitz) in the Vatican. Later Melanija returned to Lithuania and  lived in her father
2 CONC 's estate. Both her and Erelique's grandson - the son of a son of a son of a son-in-law in Italy became Apoliner. So Napoleon would be the grandfather of Apolinero.  However, this version is clearly confirmed, because until now it
