2 CONT '''Jérôme Napoléon "Bo" Bonaparte''' (5 July 1805 – 17 June 1870) was a French-American farmer, chairman of the Maryland Agricultural Society, first president of the Maryland Club,[1] and the son of Elizabeth Patterson and Jérôme 
2 CONC Bonaparte, brother of Napoleon I. 
