1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Lucien Charles Napoléon Bonaparte, 3rd Prince of Canino and Musignano, was born in Philadelphia as the son of Charles Lucien Bonaparte and his wife (and cousin), Zénaïde Bonaparte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Lucien succeeded his father as 3rd Prince of Canino and Musignano upon his death on 29 July 1857. Following the death of Joseph Lucien at the age of 41 in Rome, his brother Lucien succeeded him as 4th Prince of Canino and M
2 CONC usignano.
