1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Col. John Wise of England and Virginia (1617-1695) ; his ancestors and descendants (1918)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/coljohnwiseofeng00wise
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/coljohnwiseofeng00wise#page/26/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.26 ______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucien_Bonaparte-Wyse
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucien Napoléon Bonaparte-Wyse (13 January 1845 - 15 June 1909) was a French engineer. He was born in Paris as the son of Laetitia Bonaparte-Wyse, daughter of Lucien Bonaparte and estranged wife of the Irish politician Sir Thomas 
2 CONC Wyse, Lucien Napoléon Bonaparte-Wyse's real father was a British army officer, Captain Studholm John Hodgson.[1] He joined the French navy as a midshipman on the ship Amphion, based in Toulon. Commissioned by the French company Co
2 CONC mpagnie universelle du canal interocéanique de Panama he obtained a concession to build a canal from the Colombian government. He made two trips to Panama to study the project and the concluded it was feasible. The agreement, know
2 CONC n as the "Wyse Concession" was valid 99 years and allowed the company to dig a canal and exploit it. The Panama Scandal allowed Ferdinand de Lesseps to redeem the rights. After this Bonaparte Wyse wrote his memoirs, intending to p
2 CONC rove to investors that the project was viable. The United States would get the concession and build the canal.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Cap Brun in Cannes on 15 June 1909, at the age of 64 years.
