1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Jerome Napoleon Bonaparte II (November 5, 1830 – September 3, 1893) was a son of Jerome Napoleon Bonaparte and Susan May Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the grandnephew of Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte of France and the grandson of Jerome Bonaparte, King of Westphalia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He entered the United States Military Academy at West Point in 1848 and graduated 11th in Class of 1852. Upon graduation was commissioned a second lieutenant and served in Texas with the Mounted Rifle Regiment. His letters from Fo
2 CONC rt Inge and Fort Ewell have been preserved by the Maryland Historical Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT He resigned from the U.S. Army in August 1854 to serve in the army of his first cousin-once-removed, Napoleon III of France and was commissioned a colonel in French army. He fought in Algiers, the Italian campaign, the Crimean War
2 CONC , and the Franco-Prussian War.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871, he resigned from the French Army and returned home to the United States where he married Caroline Le Roy Appleton Edgar. They would have two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1.Louise-Eugénie Bonaparte (1873–1923), married in 1896 Count Adam Carl von Moltke-Huitfeld (1864–1944): they have numerous descendants.
2 CONT *  2.Jerome Napoleon Charles Bonaparte (1878–1945), married in 1914 Blanche Pierce Stenbeigh, daughter of Edward and Emily Pierce of Newtonville, Massachusetts, and former wife of Harold Stenbeigh of Hewlett, New York: no children
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Prides Crossing, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/41658109/jerome-napoleon-bonaparte
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerome_Napoleon_Bonaparte_II
