2 CONT Czesław Malewski, Rody i herby szlacheckie na Litwie (XV).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archiwum2000.tripod.com/522/malews.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Below we will describe an interesting story: the three famous properties of the French Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte (1769-1821), his son Napoleon II ( full name Napoleon François Charles Joseph Bonaparte ) (1811 Paris - Vienna, 1832
2 CONC ), and the famous French poet Guyom Apolinero (in French. Guillaume Apollinaire ) (1880-1918) The possible connections as well as the role here was Melanija Kostrovickaitė (Melania Kostrowicka)who was the granddaughter of Barbara 
2 CONC Sekliuckytė.
2 CONT
2 CONT The shoelaces have been associated with Kostrowitz, whose prominent representative is the famous French poet Apoliner, namely Apolinist Kostrowicki. Barbora Sekliuckytė with her second husband Samuel Kostrovickiu (1729 - 1780) had
2 CONC  a son Onufrijų ( Onufr ) (~ 1760 -?) and grandson Samuel (1788-1859). Samuel Kostrovicki and his wife, Ona Zaleskaya ( Anna Zaleska ) had a daughter named Melanie. Melanie Kostrovickaitė was educated in the literature, history, l
2 CONC anguages, music and painting. She was taken to Vienna's estate, Schloss Schönbrunn where lived the second wife of Napoleon, Napoleon second wife was Marie - Louise d'Autriche (1791 1847).
2 CONT
2 CONT Here Melanie met Napoleon and Marie Luis's son Napoleon II; the second emperor of France, who was nicknamed Ereliukas. The Napoleonic marriage with the daughter of the Austrian Emperor Francis II was purely political which sought 
2 CONC to converge with the Hapsburg dynasty and have a successor. Immediately after his birth, his son received the title of Roman king, but Napoleon in 1814 and 1815 having left him the throne of the emperor in France, did not receive 
2 CONC much approval. The state winners resisted them. Ereliukas ruled only 15 days - since 1815 June 22 until 1815 July 7. The damsel grew up in the Grandfather's Palace in Vienna where he was given Reichstadt (Reichstadt Duke's title) 
2 CONC up until 1830. Ereliukas did not know who his real father was. The hopes of Napoleon II were tied by Bonapartists but in 1830 was overthrown by King Charles X of France, Napoleon II was already too weak to take on the throne, He w
2 CONC as sick and died early (21 years old). His pompous mask is exhibited at the Vienna Schonbrunn Palace. One day Melanija and Ereliukas got acquainted. The eaglet Melanija old age is pasakojusi nephew Marcelijus (Marcin ) Kostrovicki
2 CONC ui (brother Lucian, who was married to Jozefa Sekliuckytę ( Jozefa Sieklucka ), son), it gives him not only for his oil paintings, but also drawings, watercolors and oil painted works with Reichštato Duke's signature. Melanija and
2 CONC  Erelius became lovers. Here a son was born to Melanija (who was 18 years old) born in Italy, finding herself with explainable circumstances. The kidnapper - a child of the Imperial Blood - was arranged and educated (for the money
2 CONC  of Kostriewitz) in the Vatican. Later Melanija returned to Lithuania and lived in her father's estate. Both her and Erelique's grandson - the son of a son of a son of a son-in-law in Italy became Apoliner. So Napoleon would be th
2 CONC e grandfather of Apolinero. However, this version is clearly confirmed, because until now it was argued that there are other Apolineras Kostrovickaitės (the other belonging to another family, and the coat of arms). Michael Kostrov
2 CONC ickio ( Michal Kostrowicki ) daughter Angelica (Angelika) was unmarried and had a child born in Rome, his father is not exactly known.
