1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_Pozzo_di_Borgo
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Philippe Pozzo di Borgo''' (born 14 February 1951) is a Corsican French businessman who is the Director of Pommery and was the owner of an inherited historic hôtel particulier in Paris used as a function hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Background
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe is the second son of the French duke Pozzo di Borgo and the Marquis de Vogue.[1] The noble family dates back to the 1500s.[2] After completing his education, he began working in the champagne industry. Prior to his job as
2 CONC  director of Pommery, Philippe was a manager at Moët and Chandon.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe di Borgo became a diabetic quadriplegic in 1993 following a paragliding accident. Because of his disability, he attempted to commit suicide by wrapping an oxygen tube around his neck.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://photos.geni.com/p13/7d/fb/6c/b6/5344485f16eb131b/2011_intouchables_original.jpg|right|110px}}
2 CONT
2 CONT  In popular culture
2 CONT
2 CONT The story of Philippe and his Moroccan attendant, [https://www.geni.com/people/Abdel-Sellou/6000000176811358095 Abdel Sallou], was told in a 2003 documentary, A la vie, à la mort.[4] Their story was also adapted in the ''biographi
2 CONC cal movies '''The Intouchables''' (2011)'',[5] and the Indian, Argentine, and American re-makes, respectively, Oopiri (2016), Inseparables (2016),[6] and The Upside (2017).[7] These movies were based on his memoir, A Second Wind.[
2 CONC 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
