0 @N6000000002322291299@ NOTE The Parthenopeon Republic was a short-lived republic in Naples proclaimed on
1 CONT January 23, 1799, after a popular uprising of Pro-French republicans resulting
1 CONT in the ouster of King Ferdinand IV. A counterrevolution was launched the same
1 CONT year by a papal army and an English fleet under Horatio Nelson that resulted
1 CONT in the wholesale butcheries of the republicans and the return of Ferdinand in
1 CONT 1802. In 1806, Napoleon avenged himself by invading Naples and proclaiming
1 CONT Joseph King of Naples on March 30, 1806. Ferdinand then fled to Sicily.
